# Keeps `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads to what the image actually needs: web/ and
# server/. Note that gcloud uses THIS file instead of .gitignore, which is what makes a
# deploy from a working copy work at all — the generated question bank under
# web/public/ is untracked by git but must be uploaded.
#
# Leading slashes matter. An unanchored `data/` or `tools/` would match at any depth and
# silently drop web/public/data/ (the question bank), producing a build that fails the
# prebuild guard.
.git/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/

/public/
/tools/
/data/
AZ-104_dump.pdf
